11
00:00:18.591 --> 00:00:20.426
The cold Humboldt current helps

12
00:00:20.426 --> 00:00:21.835
make the Atacama one of

13
00:00:21.835 --> 00:00:23.976
the driest places on Earth.

14
00:00:24.303 --> 00:00:25.969
Cold currents often come with

15
00:00:25.969 --> 00:00:28.325
upwelling, which brings nutrients up,

16
00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:29.121
and with them,

17
00:00:29.121 --> 00:00:29.945
fish.

18
00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:31.791
Your turn.

19
00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:33.854
Is it warm or cold?
